{"pageid": 959, "title": "Necrotype", "revid": 2221, "categories": ["Lore", "Monsters", "Necrotypes"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e2/Necrotype.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215001410\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Necrotype\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e2/Necrotype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215001410\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"181\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Necrotype.png\" data-image-key=\"Necrotype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Necrotype.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>Hunter beware, destroying the possessed human corpses of the Phantasma-Necrotype complicates any hunt, as the corpse's living relatives must never discover the truth.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">The Book of Butcher</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Necrotypes</b> are a breed of <a href=\"/wiki/Monsters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Monsters\">monster</a> fought by <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a>. Commonly referred to as \"zombies,\" they are the manifestation of the undead and revitalized corpses.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span></h2>\n<p>The Necrotype first comes from Haitian folklore,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> where the fear of being forced into slavery after death manifested the idea of zombies.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> The proliferation of Zombie media would then spread the fears across the globe, causing Necrotypes to actually form.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>Necrotypes usually follow the regular appearances, strengths and weaknesses of the common media zombie.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Classifications\">Classifications</span></h3>\n<p>There are two types of Necrotypes: Common and Phantasma.\n</p>\n<ul><li>The <b>Common Necrotype</b> is a manifestation of a fear of the undead. They must be killed according to the fear that spawned them; traditionally, this involves the destruction of the body.</li>\n<li>The <b>Phantasma-Necrotype</b> is when a <a href=\"/wiki/Phantasmatype\" title=\"Phantasmatype\">Phantasmatype</a> possesses a corpse, usually a human one. These corpses then become the Phantasmatype's tether, which must be destroyed to release the spirit.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Necrotypes\">Notable Necrotypes</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Necrotype_Totems\">Necrotype Totems</span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>TBA</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"0fbd8161c38d636aa1e8c87c1fe4fa2d\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Necrotype-png\" style=\"position: relative; height:185px; width:184px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Necrotype.png\" title=\"Necrotype.png (2.01 MB)\" style=\"height:185px; width:184px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e2/Necrotype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/184?cb=20241215001410\" title=\"Necrotype.png (2.01 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Necrotype.png\" data-image-key=\"Necrotype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\"></noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" title=\"Necrotype.png (2.01 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" alt=\"\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Necrotype.png\" data-image-key=\"Necrotype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e2/Necrotype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/184?cb=20241215001410\" /></a></div></div></div></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span></h2>\n<small><div style=\"width:auto; max-height:190px; overflow:auto; padding-left:0.5em; padding-right:0.5em; border-top-left-radius:0.5em; border-bottom-left-radius:0.5em\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOB_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOB_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOB_1-2\">1.2</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">Tynion, James IV</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">Book of Butcher</a>,</i> vol. #1, <a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">issue no.1</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>, 2023.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Wilentz, Amy (26 October 2012). <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2012/10/31/opinion/a-zombie-is-a-slave-forever.html\">\"A Zombie is a Slave Forever\"</a>. <i>The New York Times.</i> Haiti. Retrieved 31 October 2012.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Wilentz, Amy (December 2011). <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://amywilentz.com/response-to-i-walked-with-a-zombie/\">\"Response to 'I Walked with a Zombie'\"</a>. <i>amywilentz.com</i> Retrieved 2 February 2018.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div></small></div>", "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T22:43:34+00:00"}